From: Alex Scotti <alexscotti@gmail.com>
Subject: Bluray: do not read every playlist when a disc is opened

Open() called bd_get_titles(), which opens and parses every .mpls in
BDMV/PLAYLIST. A player that follows the disc's navigation opens a playlist
only when the disc selects it, and our file server reads a playlist open as
"this title was chosen", so a disc open looked like every title being chosen
at once.

The list had two readers. GetTitleLongest() picked a title for a disc whose
First Play cannot be played; that disc now fails to open with the error it
already logged. DiscHasDolbyVision() walked the list to engage the Dolby
Vision output for the whole disc session; with it gone no session is engaged,
so each segment plays in its own format. A Dolby Vision title is still
detected per stream, from the STN table of the playlist being played.

The session code in AMLUtils, AMLCodec and VideoPlayer is left in place. It is
inert while no session is set, and leaving it keeps this patch small.

